# Secrets: exclude env files at EVERY depth, not only the context root.
# A bare `.env` pattern matches the root file only — `apps/api/.env`, which
# README tells developers to create and which holds JWT_SECRET / DATABASE_URL,
# was still entering the build context and being baked into the API image by
# `COPY apps/api apps/api`. The `**/` variants are what actually exclude it,
# mirroring the `**/node_modules` and `**/dist` entries above.
# Guarded by tests/repo-invariants.test.ts. See docs/security/encryption-at-rest.md.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Committed *.example files hold placeholders only and are safe to ship.
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example
